  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["D25", "D30", "D47"],
      "pins": ["D25.2", "D30.2", "D47.2"],
      "nets": ["/NET0189"],
      "observed": "The anodes of the three discrete status LEDs D25 (green), D30 (green) and D47 (yellow) are tied together on net /NET0189, which contains only those three nodes and connects to no supply or other component. Their cathodes go through R38/R95/R47 to CM4 outputs (PI_nLED_Activity, Ethernet_nLED2, Ethernet_nLED3), but the anode rail is floating, so no current path exists.",
      "expected": "LED anodes must be connected to a supply rail (+3V3) so the LEDs can light when the CM4 pulls the cathode side low; other LEDs on the board (e.g. D29, D20, D9) have their anodes/pull-ups tied to +3V3, and the spec describes these as intended status indicators.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"41\") (name \"/NET0189\") ... (node (ref \"D25\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"A\")) (node (ref \"D30\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"A\")) (node (ref \"D47\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"A\")))"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"1\") (name \"+3V3\") ... (node (ref \"D29\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"A\")) ...)"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "Addressable status LEDs (WS2812B, D5-D7, D18-D21) ... and an analog switch ... for LED/signal routing."}
      ],
      "impact": "The Ethernet link/activity and Pi-activity indicator LEDs (D25, D30, D47) can never illuminate, so link and activity status is silently lost; the rest of the board's behaviour is unaffected.",
      "confidence": 0.6
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The build otherwise matches the specification (16 MHz MCP2515 crystals Y3/Y5, SM712 TVS arrays D1/D46 on the CAN pairs, isolated CAN transceivers U18/U29, LTC4412 ideal-diode path U26+Q11, direct switch on Global_EN). The one clear deviation is that the common anode rail of status LEDs D25/D30/D47 (net /NET0189) is left unconnected to +3V3, leaving those LEDs permanently dark."
}

